=== AB7: zero-padding inertness over the WHOLE nu<=6 enumerated class ===
  E=0   base lists tested : 964
  E>=1  base lists tested : 1745   (= S(1..6) = 0+3+24+110+397+1211 = 1745)
  paddings per list       : (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 13)
  (list, padding) pairs   : 18963
  PADDING-DEPENDENT STEP COUNTS : 0

  Reason (unchanged, and this is what carries the general case): at each step
  the block is the d LARGEST non-head entries, so a zero can enter the block
  only when fewer than d positive entries remain -- and in that case the run
  aborts whether or not the zeros were written down.

